# Build context for frontend/Dockerfile only (BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore
# in place of the root one). The build stage does `COPY . .`, so anything left in
# here becomes an input to `npm run build`: a backend-only change, or any commit
# at all via .git, would otherwise rebuild the frontend for nothing.
.git
.github
.claude
**/node_modules
dist
backend
e2e
*.md
LICENSE
docker-compose.yml
# A host copy would let `tsc -b` decide the project is up to date and skip the check.
*.tsbuildinfo
